cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Tanakh Reader: A Colometric Reading Edition of the Hebrew Bible"
authors:
  - name: "Stan the Bible Man"
    email: "thebibleman77@gmail.com"
date-released: "2026-05-10"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bibleman-stan/readers-tanakh"
url: "https://tanakh-reader.com"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A colometric reading edition of the Hebrew Bible based on the Tiberian
  Masoretic Text in its Leningrad recension. Each line renders one
  atomic thought unit (ATU) motivated by Hebrew grammatical and prosodic
  structure. The edition is produced via the ATU apparatus (atu-method)
  — a proposition-first generative framework with structural
  justifications, merge-overrides, and morpho-syntactic validation
  against Macula-Hebrew (lowfat XML treebank) and BHSA/ETCBC syntactic
  annotations. The te'amim (Masoretic cantillation accents) are
  preserved in the source text for textual fidelity but play no role in
  editorial decisions (canon §1, retired 2026-05-05).
keywords:
  - Hebrew Bible
  - Tanakh
  - colometric edition
  - reading edition
  - atomic thought unit
  - ATU
  - sense-lines
  - Masoretic Text
  - Leningrad Codex
references:
  - type: software
    title: "ATU Method: Computational Colometry for Canonical Texts"
    authors:
      - name: "Stan the Bible Man"
        email: "thebibleman77@gmail.com"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/bibleman-stan/atu-method"
    notes: "Methodology and apparatus used to produce this edition."
  - type: data
    title: "STEPBible TAHOT (Translators Amalgamated Hebrew OT)"
    notes: "Primary Hebrew source text, CC-BY-4.0"
    url: "https://github.com/STEPBible/STEPBible-Data"
  - type: data
    title: "Macula Hebrew"
    notes: "Clear Bible's lowfat XML treebank for Hebrew Bible"
    url: "https://github.com/Clear-Bible/macula-hebrew"
  - type: data
    title: "Open Scriptures Hebrew Bible"
    notes: "Westminster Leningrad Codex morphology, CC-BY-4.0"
    url: "https://github.com/openscriptures/morphhb"
